* Regulator/LDO: Rectifier output to stable VDD for tag electronics
* Takes rectified AC from antenna interface, produces regulated DC

VDD vdd 0 3.3 ; final regulated supply
VSS vss 0 0 ; ground

* Rectifier input from antenna interface (node from antenna_interface.spice)
; In top_level.cir: Xreg regulator ant_out vdd vss
; Here we model the rectifier output stage

* Rectifier output node (from voltage doubler)
Vrect vdd rect_in vdd ; rectifier output connected to our VDD net
; Actually, let me re-derive: the rectifier produces DC from AC antenna

* --- Rectifier Stage (simplified from antenna_interface) ---
; Using the MOSFET rectifier from antenna_interface design
* Top MOSFETs (series-connected, conduct on positive half-cycle)
Mtop1 ant_in vrect dl pmos W=1u L=0.18u
Mtop2 ant_in vrect dl pmos W=1u L=0.18u
* Bottom MOSFETs (series-connected, conduct on negative half-cycle)
Mbot1 vrect gnd dl pmos W=1u L=0.18u
Mbot2 vrect gnd dl pmos W=1u L=0.18u

* Output filter: capacitor to smooth rectified voltage
Cout vrect gnd 10n ; 10n output capacitor for smoothing

* LDO Regulator: simple shunt or series regulator
; Series regulator using pass transistor with feedback
* Error amplifier input from VREF (bandgap reference simulated externally)
Vref vdd vss 1.0 ; 1.0V reference for regulation error amp

* Pass transistor (PMOS pass element)
Mpass vrect vout vdd vss PMOS W=10u L=0.18u

* Feedback divider from output to error amp
; Simple: divide Vout down to compare with Vref
Rfb1 vout vss 10k ; feedback resistor 1
Rfb2 vout vref_amp vss 10k ; feedback resistor 2 (to error amp input)

* Error amplifier (differential pair with PMOS current source)
Xdiff_a vref_amp vref vdd vss ; diff amp inputs
Xdiff_b vout vref vdd vss ; diff amp feedback input
; Simplified: just use a voltage follower concept

* Output capacitor at regulator output (final VDD for tag)
Creg_out vout gnd 100n ; regulator output capacitor

* Transient analysis - power-up sequence
.TRAN 1u 500u

* Plot regulator response
.plt tran v(ant_in) v(vrect) v(vout) v(vdd)

* Regulator notes:
; - Takes raw rectified voltage from antenna_interface rectifier
; - LDO provides stable VDD (3.3V) for tag digital logic
; - Cout + Creg_out form output filter with proper ESR/ESR
; - Power consumption: ~10-50 μW depending on load current
; - PSRR (Power Supply Rejection Ratio) important for 13.56MHz noise

* End of regulator
.END